Bugne build-time patch for sendspin-cpp 0.7.2, applied by the top-level
CMakeLists.txt at configure time (managed_components is gitignored and
re-fetched on clean builds).

Since 0.7.0 the library handles the ESP-IDF WebSocket handshake natively
(it registers its handler as ws_post_handshake_cb and its Kconfig selects
HTTPD_WS_POST_HANDSHAKE_CB_SUPPORT), so the 0.6.1-era handshake fix is gone.
One local fix remains: the library never sets the httpd task stack size, so
it inherits the 4 KB HTTPD_DEFAULT_CONFIG default. The open/close callbacks
(C++ shared_ptr + std::function) and the async frame sends all run on that
task, and 4 KB corrupts the LWIP select semaphore under load (bench-proven
crash: assert "taking semaphore failed"). Give it 8 KB.

--- a/src/esp/ws_server.cpp
+++ b/src/esp/ws_server.cpp
@@ -60,7 +60,11 @@

     // Configure the HTTP server
     httpd_config_t config = HTTPD_DEFAULT_CONFIG();
+    // Bugne: the default 4 KB httpd task stack is tight; the open/close callbacks
+    // (C++ shared_ptr + std::function) and the async frame sends all run on this
+    // task, and 4 KB corrupts the LWIP select semaphore under load.
+    config.stack_size = 8192;
     if (task_stack_in_psram) {
         config.task_caps = MALLOC_CAP_SPIRAM;
     }
     config.task_priority = task_priority;
